{"id":"Prowl.PaperUI.PaperCursor","name":"PaperCursor","display":"PaperCursor","kind":"enum","assembly":"Prowl.Paper","namespace":"Prowl.PaperUI","outer":null,"signature":"public enum PaperCursor","bases":[],"docs":{"summary":"A hardware mouse cursor shape an element requests while hovered. Paper only resolves which shape the pointer is over (see [`CurrentCursor`](#api~Prowl.PaperUI.Paper~CurrentCursor) / [`OnCursorChange`](#api~Prowl.PaperUI.Paper~OnCursorChange)); the host application maps the value to its windowing library and sets the OS cursor. The names mirror the common cross-platform standard set (GLFW / SDL); a host should fall back to [`Default`](#api~Prowl.PaperUI.PaperCursor~Default) for any shape it doesn't provide."},"attributes":[],"members":[{"kind":"value","name":"Inherit","signature":"Inherit = 0","docs":{"summary":"No explicit cursor; inherit from the parent (resolves to [`Default`](#api~Prowl.PaperUI.PaperCursor~Default) at the root)."},"static":false,"obsolete":false,"line":234,"path":"Paper/Paper/Enums.cs","anchor":"Inherit"},{"kind":"value","name":"Default","signature":"Default","docs":{"summary":"The standard arrow cursor."},"static":false,"obsolete":false,"line":237,"path":"Paper/Paper/Enums.cs","anchor":"Default"},{"kind":"value","name":"Pointer","signature":"Pointer","docs":{"summary":"Pointing hand, for clickable elements (links, buttons)."},"static":false,"obsolete":false,"line":240,"path":"Paper/Paper/Enums.cs","anchor":"Pointer"},{"kind":"value","name":"Grab","signature":"Grab","docs":{"summary":"Open hand, for something grabbable that isn't being dragged yet."},"static":false,"obsolete":false,"line":243,"path":"Paper/Paper/Enums.cs","anchor":"Grab"},{"kind":"value","name":"Grabbing","signature":"Grabbing","docs":{"summary":"Closed hand, for something currently being dragged."},"static":false,"obsolete":false,"line":246,"path":"Paper/Paper/Enums.cs","anchor":"Grabbing"},{"kind":"value","name":"Text","signature":"Text","docs":{"summary"